---
title: 'Status Bar'
enterprise: true
---

The Status Bar shows the values of the hovered datum for every series in a cartesian chart, in a single row of label and value pairs.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Status Bar" name="enabling-status-bar" type="generated" /%}

## Enabling the Status Bar

To show the Status Bar, set `statusBar.enabled` to `true`:

```js format="snippet"
{
    statusBar: {
        enabled: true,
    },
}
```

In this example:

- Hovering the chart shows the value of every series at the hovered category.
- Each value is labelled with the series' `yName` and formatted with the root `formatter`, as the axis formats it.
- Each value is coloured as the series draws the datum, including any `itemStyler` colour.
- When nothing is hovered, the Status Bar shows the last datum of each series.

## Position and Inactive State

By default, the Status Bar is shown above the series area, aligned to its start. Use `position` to place it elsewhere, in the same way as the [Legend](./legend/#placement). A floating Status Bar is drawn over the chart rather than taking space from it.

Use `inactive` to choose what the Status Bar shows when nothing is hovered:

- `'last'`: the last datum of each series. This is the default.
- `'recent'`: the most recently hovered datum, or the last datum before any hover.
- `'hidden'`: nothing; the Status Bar is hidden until a datum is hovered.

```js format="snippet"
{
    statusBar: {
        enabled: true,
        position: { placement: 'bottom', floating: false },
        inactive: 'recent',
        border: { enabled: true },
        cornerRadius: 4,
        padding: 6,
    },
}
```

{% chartExampleRunner title="Status Bar Position" name="status-bar-position" type="generated" /%}

The Status Bar can be styled with `fill`, `fillOpacity`, `border`, `cornerRadius` and `padding`, and its text with the `label` and `value` options.

When the items exceed `maxWidth`, they wrap onto further lines according to `wrapping`. Lines that exceed `maxHeight` are dropped, and with `truncate` enabled the last visible value ends with an ellipsis.

## Renderer

Use a `renderer` to choose the items the Status Bar shows. It receives the `values` collected from every series at the hovered category, and whether they come from a hovered datum (`active`). It returns a list of items, each with an optional `label` and a `value`, or a single text value. To colour a value, return it as text segments, for example `[{ text: formattedValue, color }]`.

```js format="snippet"
{
    statusBar: {
        enabled: true,
        renderer: ({ values, active }) => [
            { label: active ? 'Month' : 'Latest', value: values[0]?.datum.month },
            ...values.map(({ label, formattedValue }) => ({ label, value: formattedValue })),
        ],
    },
}
```

{% chartExampleRunner title="Status Bar Renderer" name="status-bar-renderer" type="generated" /%}

In this example:

- The first item shows the hovered month, or `Latest` when nothing is hovered.
- The last item shows the average of the collected values.

The `renderer` runs when the hovered datum changes, and when the chart's data or options change.

## Series Collectors

Each series collects the values it contributes to the Status Bar. By default, these are the series' value keys, such as `yKey`, labelled with their names, such as `yName`.

Use the series `collector` to change them. It receives the `datum` and the default `values`, and returns the values to use, or `undefined` to keep the defaults.

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'bar',
            xKey: 'quarter',
            yKey: 'revenue',
            yName: 'Revenue',
            collector: ({ datum, values }) => [
                ...values,
                { key: 'margin', label: 'Margin', value: (datum.revenue - datum.costs) / datum.revenue },
            ],
        },
    ],
}
```

{% chartExampleRunner title="Series Collector" name="series-collector" type="generated" /%}

A value bound to an axis is formatted as the axis formats it. Set `formattedValue` on any other value to control its text, and `color` to change its colour.

The `collector` runs only while the Status Bar is enabled, at the same times as the `renderer`.

